---

<ContentLayout
  title="Chest Workouts — Build a Stronger Upper Body"
  h1="Chest Workouts"
  description="Free chest workout guide with effective exercises, sample routines, and form tips for building chest strength and muscle."
  path="/workouts/chest-workouts/"
  lead="Build chest strength with push-ups, presses, flyes, and smart progression."
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Why train chest?</h2>
  <p>Chest training improves pushing strength, upper-body muscle balance, posture, and overall gym performance. A strong chest also supports better pressing mechanics for shoulders and triceps.</p>

  <h2>Best chest exercises</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Push-ups:</strong> a simple bodyweight movement that works chest, shoulders, triceps, and core.</li>
    <li><strong>Dumbbell press:</strong> allows a natural range of motion and easy progression.</li>
    <li><strong>Incline press:</strong> emphasizes the upper chest and shoulders.</li>
    <li><strong>Cable or band flyes:</strong> add constant tension for chest development.</li>
    <li><strong>Dips:</strong> a challenging compound movement for advanced lifters.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Simple chest workout routine</h2>
  <p>Do 2–4 sets of each exercise:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Push-ups: 8–15 reps</li>
    <li>Dumbbell press: 8–12 reps</li>
    <li>Incline press: 8–12 reps</li>
    <li>Cable or band flyes: 10–15 reps</li>
    <li>Optional dips: 6–10 reps</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Form tips</h2>
  <p>Keep your shoulder blades gently pulled back and down, lower under control, and press through the full range of motion. Do not bounce the weight or let your shoulders round forward.</p>
</ContentLayout>
